#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087688 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087435 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/id #uuid "88c5f90c-9bf9-58a2-a9a2-7c7ff1fc4f8a" :question/math-academy-id "e-14370" :question/problem "The lines $y=2x$ and $kx-2y=-1$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y=2x$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $2$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx-2y=-1$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n$kx - 2y|=-1; - 2y|=-kx - 1; 2y|= kx + 1; y|= \\frac{k}{2}x + \\frac{1}{2}$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{2}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{2}=2\n$$\n\nConsequently, $k=4$."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050622}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478529 :question-generator/id #uuid "553548b2-9ae8-58f6-93d0-49b58d622766" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186087688.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088067 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "60eba464-c836-5e56-8019-94413acf4ad6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085128}] :question/id #uuid "8fe6d174-341f-5856-be44-1861285e1986" :question/math-academy-id "q-214098" :question/problem "The lines $y = 2x + 5$ and $kx + 3y = 9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088068 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "ad8dd299-34e2-51c8-9ba6-9b32de88cb92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085129}] :question/id #uuid "93f5de54-6bcd-5688-b2b5-e060b8822757" :question/math-academy-id "q-214099" :question/problem "The lines $8x - 2y =-2$ and $kx - 5y = 15$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478499 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d64d33c3-8ae5-5650-9976-22a54c0377ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d64d33c3-8ae5-5650-9976-22a54c0377ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478528} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c379fc8-7257-5c47-9efa-e0f9d6f826a3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04208a31-b2ae-567f-8896-e86342d6ce9d" :question/problem "The lines $-21x - 12y = 108$ and $kx + 3y = 9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $-21x - 12y = 108$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n-21x - 12y = 108\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -12y = 21x + 108\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = - \\frac{7}{4}x - 9.\n$$\nIts slope is $- \\frac{7}{4}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 3y = 9$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 3y = 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 3y = -kx + 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{3}x + 3.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{3}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{3}=- \\frac{7}{4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-3$ gives $k=\\frac{21}{4}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478500 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b18772b2-e66f-5bbd-9b15-c5c090edd671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b18772b2-e66f-5bbd-9b15-c5c090edd671" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{48}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478524} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ce38150-54c5-55d5-a002-94896d315fb1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478510}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "211d09f0-9544-5c60-a27a-1e3939da787d" :question/problem "The lines $24x - 10y = 70$ and $kx + 4y = 12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $24x - 10y = 70$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n24x - 10y = 70\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -10y = -24x + 70\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{12}{5}x - 7.\n$$\nIts slope is $\\frac{12}{5}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 4y = 12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 4y = 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 4y = -kx + 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{4}x + 3.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{4}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{4}=\\frac{12}{5}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-4$ gives $k=- \\frac{48}{5}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc4e6c7-209b-59fb-9cfe-0fd922736040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bc4e6c7-209b-59fb-9cfe-0fd922736040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "63" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478504} :answer-field/id #uuid "a02203b1-03c9-52de-9223-ab83694649cb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478522}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b6bd912-687a-541d-a6c5-b5a879018279" :question/problem "The lines $y = -7x + 0$ and $kx + 9y = -5$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = -7x + 0$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-7$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 9y = -5$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 9y = -5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 9y = -kx - 5\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{9}x - \\frac{5}{9}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{9}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{9}=-7.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-9$ gives $k=63$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ba1d3b5-6fee-59da-8756-7de1193bec63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478520}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba1d3b5-6fee-59da-8756-7de1193bec63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478520} :answer-field/id #uuid "65aee0d1-2854-5e0c-93eb-7b4cd98f7548" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4dafc1fb-015c-56ff-bc14-52effb959f64" :question/problem "The lines $x - 4y = 48$ and $kx - 4y = 12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $x - 4y = 48$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nx - 4y = 48\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = -x + 48\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{1}{4}x - 12.\n$$\nIts slope is $\\frac{1}{4}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 4y = 12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 4y = 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = -kx + 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{4}x - 3.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{4}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $4$ gives $k=1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478514 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7629e520-1dca-5eb9-886c-d80b56572f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478515}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7629e520-1dca-5eb9-886c-d80b56572f75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478515} :answer-field/id #uuid "31b237ac-5c01-5409-9ef0-ff8e53ffc363" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478505}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72dbd957-6f59-540e-9ca7-2b36673b5f34" :question/problem "The lines $y = 3x + 6$ and $kx - 6y = -9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = 3x + 6$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $3$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 6y = -9$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 6y = -9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -6y = -kx - 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{6}x + \\frac{3}{2}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{6}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{6}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $6$ gives $k=18$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478516 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d995a2b-c1a5-5298-b2cc-a203c0911775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d995a2b-c1a5-5298-b2cc-a203c0911775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{49}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478511} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4a978e5-f5fa-5ed7-8053-be55abcb58b3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478527}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "889f6a39-9b44-51a3-bbee-eb6f0f8b4ebb" :question/problem "The lines $14x - 4y = -36$ and $kx - 7y = 0$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $14x - 4y = -36$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n14x - 4y = -36\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = -14x - 36\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{7}{2}x + 9.\n$$\nIts slope is $\\frac{7}{2}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 7y = 0$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 7y = 0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -7y = -kx + 0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{7}x + 0.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{7}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{7}=\\frac{7}{2}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $7$ gives $k=\\frac{49}{2}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25484164-d56b-55cd-8788-5f282b6ba98e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478501}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25484164-d56b-55cd-8788-5f282b6ba98e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478501} :answer-field/id #uuid "7185e834-19ec-520c-872e-0e6e2b05f0ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478513}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f6b69ef-4822-5ea0-bc5a-d5e5650a7779" :question/problem "The lines $y = 5x + 12$ and $kx - 9y = 12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = 5x + 12$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $5$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 9y = 12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 9y = 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -9y = -kx + 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{9}x - \\frac{4}{3}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{9}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{9}=5.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $9$ gives $k=45$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43e9a804-9f59-5019-9aa3-60392ef8ca28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43e9a804-9f59-5019-9aa3-60392ef8ca28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{55}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478507} :answer-field/id #uuid "41021883-e0b3-57c5-b984-0654400ffc7f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478506}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8fb31242-a4bd-58a8-a20e-be804320d787" :question/problem "The lines $-11x - 4y = 40$ and $kx + 5y = -11$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- To find the slope of the line $-11x - 4y = 40$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\n-11x - 4y = 40\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -4y = 11x + 40\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = - \\frac{11}{4}x - 10.\n$$\nIts slope is $- \\frac{11}{4}$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx + 5y = -11$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx + 5y = -11\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad 5y = -kx - 11\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = -\\frac{k}{5}x - \\frac{11}{5}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $-\\dfrac{k}{5}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{k}{5}=- \\frac{11}{4}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $-5$ gives $k=\\frac{55}{4}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c51d48f2-5613-5970-9e1b-d863e0b2dac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c51d48f2-5613-5970-9e1b-d863e0b2dac3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478525} :answer-field/id #uuid "586b5446-0fe2-578a-878e-705eabf2af1b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a61ea21a-7ad8-549d-9c90-07bcff7c3c3a" :question/problem "The lines $y = -12x + 6$ and $kx - 6y = -12$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = -12x + 6$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $-12$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 6y = -12$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 6y = -12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -6y = -kx - 12\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{6}x + 2.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{6}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{6}=-12.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $6$ gives $k=-72$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478526 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "43401830-730c-57d7-8831-9a0580042ffe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27d765c0-4e75-5cf5-a4ad-5543fa562189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27d765c0-4e75-5cf5-a4ad-5543fa562189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478502} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3a3128-a0b1-5e8f-9bdd-a028e9910c0f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478517}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c691dbfe-adde-5dd9-8252-c74d417e06a8" :question/problem "The lines $y = 2x + 2$ and $kx - 5y = 9$ are parallel. What is the value of $k$?$k =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "For two lines to be parallel, they must have the same slope.\n\n- The line $y = 2x + 2$ is in slope-intercept form, and its slope is $2$.\n- To find the slope of the line $kx - 5y = 9$, we convert to slope-intercept form:\n\n$$\nkx - 5y = 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad -5y = -kx + 9\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad y = \\frac{k}{5}x - \\frac{9}{5}.\n$$\nIn slope-intercept form, the slope is the $x$-coefficient. So, the slope is $\\dfrac{k}{5}$.\n\nSince the slopes of the two lines must be equal, we must have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{k}{5}=2.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $5$ gives $k=10$."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding Unknown Parameters"}]}
